Here is a structured overview and requirements specification for the **Requirement Analysis Phase** of [LegalEase-AI-Powered-Legal-Document-Generator](https://github.com/divyasrins2007-ux/LegalEase-AI-Powered-Legal-Document-Generator?utm_source=gemini):

---

## 1. Functional Requirements

### Core User Features

* **Authentication & User Management:** Secure login/signup, role-based access control (Individual, Business, Legal Administrator), and user profile management.
* **Template Library:** Pre-defined, legally compliant contract templates (e.g., Non-Disclosure Agreements, Employment Contracts, Freelance Service Agreements, Lease Agreements).
* **Dynamic Questionnaire Interface:** Adaptive form fields that show or hide inputs based on conditional logic (e.g., jurisdiction, non-compete options, payment terms).
* **AI-Assisted Contract Drafting & Modification:** Natural language prompting to edit specific clauses or adjust parameters (e.g., *"Change termination notice to 30 days"*).
* **Document Summarization & Risk Analysis:** Automated AI analysis generating plain-English summaries and flagging high-risk clauses before final signature.
* **Multi-Format Exporting:** Ability to preview and export finalized contracts into editable `.docx` and printable `.pdf` formats.

---

## 2. Non-Functional Requirements

* **Performance & Latency:** Document generation and conversational edits must complete in under 5 seconds; intake form updates should respond seamlessly with zero UI lag.
* **Security & Data Privacy:** Full encryption of user inputs and documents both in transit (TLS 1.3) and at rest (AES-256). Compliance with data protection standards (GDPR / CCPA). User inputs must not be used for public model training.
* **Scalability:** System architecture must support concurrent document rendering jobs without latency spikes.
* **Usability & Accessibility:** Clean, accessible UI complying with WCAG 2.1 AA standards, optimized for mobile, tablet, and desktop views.

---

## 3. Technical & System Constraints

* **Third-Party API Dependency:** Dependency on LLM providers (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic) requires robust rate limit handling and fallback mechanisms.
* **Formatting Integrity:** Exported files (`.pdf` and `.docx`) must preserve consistent font styles, margins, and page numbering across different environments.
* **Legal Disclaimer & Compliance:** Software must enforce UI watermarks and disclaimer banners asserting that generated outputs are automated tools and do not constitute formal legal counsel.
